[00:14.92]Read the story about an elephant family and find out how we can improve the situation of animals in danger.阅读这个大象家庭的故事，了解我们如何改善濒危动物的处境。
[00:24.85]One Family, Two Worlds: An Elephant Story.一个家庭，两个世界：一头大象的故事。
[00:31.81]I'm now very old, and near the end of my life.我现在已经很老了，生命也即将走到尽头。
[00:37.31]But I can still remember many, many years ago, I lived with my mother, aunts and cousins in a wild and beautiful land.但我依然记得很多很多年前，我和妈妈、阿姨们还有表亲们住在一片荒凉而美丽的土地上。
[00:48.74]We enjoyed our time under the deep blue sky.我们在湛蓝的天空下享受着时光。
[00:53.32]We had more than enough to eat.我们有充足的食物。
[00:56.43]We never worried about anything until one day when I was about 3.我们从不担心任何事，直到有一天, 那时我大约3岁。
[01:03.09]On that day, a group of two-legged strangers appeared in front of us.那天，一群两条腿的陌生人出现在我们面前。
[01:10.08]I found out later that they were humans.后来我才知道他们是人类。
[01:14.25]Without warning, they raised their guns and shot dead my mother and several of my relatives.毫无征兆地，他们举起枪，打死了我的妈妈和几位亲戚。
[01:22.65]As I was about to be shot, one of them said: "Keep that little one. He's handsome, and seems smart. We can make greater use of him."就在我即将被开枪射杀时，其中一个人说：“留下那只小家伙。他很英俊，看起来也很聪明，我们能更好地利用他。”
[01:37.03]I was then trained and forced to do all kinds of stupid tricks to make humans laugh.之后我被训练，还被迫做各种愚蠢的特技来逗人类发笑。
[01:44.35]Now, years and years later, things are changing for the better.如今，许多年过去了，情况正在好转。
[01:52.45]Our population is starting to grow again.我们的数量又开始增长了。
[01:56.50]My great-great-grandsons and granddaughters are able to move freely across the land.我的曾曾孙辈们可以在这片土地上自由活动。
[02:04.51]They search for food, water and places to rest.他们寻找食物、水和休息的地方。
[02:09.69]The little ones sometimes damage crops and people's homes.小家伙们有时会破坏庄稼和人们的房屋。
[02:15.24]But they are not chased or harmed.但他们不会被追赶或伤害。
[02:19.45]There are no angry humans going after them.没有愤怒的人类追捕他们。
[02:23.68]Instead, people leave them bags of corn and fruit on the roadside.相反，人们会在路边给他们留下一袋袋玉米和水果。
[02:30.00]The food leads them in the right direction back to their homeland.这些食物指引着他们回到自己的家园。
[02:35.56]Drones follow their progress, and volunteers protect them from harm.无人机追踪着他们的行踪，志愿者们保护他们免受伤害。
[02:42.32]The little ones do not have to worry about anything.小家伙们无需担心任何事。
[02:47.35]They move around without a care in the world.他们无忧无虑地四处活动。
[02:51.56]They eat when they are hungry, and sleep when tired.饿了就吃，累了就睡。
[02:57.01]They swim in the river and play when they feel like it.想玩的时候就去河里游泳、嬉戏。
[03:01.71]No one forces them to move away from their land.没有人强迫他们离开自己的土地。
[03:06.25]What a different world this is!这是一个多么不同的世界啊！
[03:09.34]This is a world of harmony between man and other animals.这是一个人类与其他动物和谐共处的世界。
[03:15.16]In the old world, we were killed for our tusks.在过去的世界里，我们因为象牙而被杀害。
[03:20.33]In this new world, humans respect and value all animal species.在这个新的世界里，人类尊重并珍视所有的动物物种。

